Z||000000||batboy||06-05-2000||12:29 PM||||I know this is way off topic, but I just have to brag about how good the Todd show was in Kansas City on June 2, 2000. It was AWESOME! Todd totally ROCKED! Every concert portrays a different side to Todd and this time he was Todd the guitar superhero. It was the power trio with just Todd, Kasum, and Trey on drums. Todd wailed and axed and put on a great show. I especially enjoyed "Black and White", "One World", "Hammer In My Heart", "Love In Action", "Buffalo Grass" and the specially done "Bang On a Drum All Day" solo on the ukulele (he called it an old Hawaiian war chant). My good friends and long time Todd fans, Wayne and Jan, had "after show passes" because they were contest runners up. They got to talk to Todd and got their Todd 'n' me pic, plus they both got their passes autographed, those lucky dogs!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.roadkill.com/~todd/pictures/gallery/bb-Todd-band.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||06-05-2000||03:03 PM||||Excellent! I didn't know that Todd still toured. What was the venue? Not that I would recognize anything you named. Just wondered if he was filling arenas or if it was a small concert hall.||||reg||1
