Z||000004||batboy||06-06-2000||08:29 PM||||Todd usually plays little places nowadays. I saw him at a 1000 person capacity club in KC. Although he doesn't draw huge crowds anymore, the ones that do go see him are generally long-time, rabid, hard-core fans. Standard, if you are not joking, I'm goin' hold you down and tickle you until you promise to listen to some of his music...LOL. The "Todd Rundgren Connection" page is down right now, but if you search on that later, it lists the concert calendar for this Todd power trio 2000 tour and various reviews and pics of the previous shows. The above pic that I took and another one of my pics (a close up of Todd) are on that website too. Warning: this tour is high energy rock 'n' roll with blazing guitar riffs! Many remember Todd has lots of electronic "spacey" songs and lots of mellow ballads, but you will only hear a couple mellow tunes this time around. I was right up front, about three rows back from center stage and my left ear is still ringing, even four days later, but I'm getting old.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 06-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||06-07-2000||01:12 AM||||In case anyone wants to see Todd on this tour, here is the calendar and reviews.<P> <A HREF="http://www.roadkill.com/todd/tour/t2000" TARGET=_blank>http://www.roadkill.com/todd/tour/t2000</A> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.roadkill.com/~todd/pictures/gallery/bb-Todd-Percy.jpg"> ||||reg||1
